p.src:
We write annual savings as $S=sY,$ where $s$ is the savings rate. The transcript-backed range is $s\in[0.10,0.20].$ The same exchange mentions income of roughly $Y\approx \$70{,}000 \hbox{ to } \$80{,}000.$ So the corresponding annual savings range is $\begin{aligned}
S_{\min} &=0.10(\$70{,}000)=\$7{,}000,\\
S_{\max} &=0.20(\$80{,}000)=\$16{,}000.\end{aligned}$

