A restaurant operator gives the simplest operating principle: 90 percent of success is showing up. He explains the phrase. If you show up to work, you get work done, and people trust you. They know you will be there like clockwork. Reliability converts time into trust: $\hbox{repeated presence}
\longrightarrow
\hbox{trust}
\longrightarrow
\hbox{opportunity}.$ This is not a law of nature. It is the mechanism the speaker describes.

